## Alternative: Keep but Mark as Deprecated

If uncertain, you can keep the files but add deprecation warnings:

```dart
// At top of each schema file:

/// DEPRECATED: This collection appears unused in the codebase.
/// Marked for removal after verification.
/// Last checked: 2026-02-03
/// If you're using this collection, please update this comment.
@Deprecated('Collection appears unused - verify before using')
class AddPlayersRecord extends FirestoreRecord {
  // ... existing code ...
}
```

This allows the schema to remain but signals to developers that it should be verified.

---

**Decision Required**: Choose one approach:
- ❌ **Full Deletion** - If ALL verifications pass
- ⚠️ **Archive** - If uncertain but likely unused
- ✅ **Keep with Warning** - If uncertain and want to be safe
- ⛔ **Do Nothing** - If any verification fails

---

**Recommended Approach**: Archive (Option B) until you can verify with team/product.
